  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Execution under N0–R3",
      "items": [
        "N0: run the complete host-native lifecycle, bypassing the common RAC phase loop.",
        "R1: add EpisodeRunner and SharedNet communication while retaining the native successor.",
        "R2: match open issues against capability tags using the shared rule-based policy.",
        "R3: add scoped work contracts and artifact evidence checks; supported, refuted and inconclusive verdicts become feedback for the next cycle."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "State, authority and stopping",
      "items": [
        "HostBridge translates native state and invokes native roles; SharedPolicy owns the common coordination rules.",
        "Each episode selects one host; the three upstream dependency stacks run in separate images.",
        "R3 verdicts retain research state and enter the next role's context. Budgets, hop limits, native terminal states and fatal provider errors govern stopping.",
        "The three adapters represent alternative integrations, not three systems jointly executing one episode."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Independent benchmark evaluation",
      "items": [
        "Hosts receive only the public task, data/ and related_work/. target_study is neither copied nor mounted into their environment.",
        "The independent score command invokes ResearchClawBench and uses the configured external judge.",
        "R3's in-loop verifier and the final benchmark judge have separate responsibilities.",
        "scores/ preserves each scoring attempt and its provenance. score.json references the current attempt; scoring infrastructure failures retain null scores and errors."
      ]
    }
  ]
